# Four independent habits in one query: four errors, and applying the fixes gives a program that parses.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv'
| where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
| render columnchart
| take 10
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..93
  PIPELINE@0..92
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..61
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..61
        BIN_EXPR@26..46
          NAME_REF@26..36
            IDENT@26..36 "customerId"
          WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
          EQ@37..38 "="
          WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
          LITERAL@39..46
            STRING@39..46 "\"c-001\""
        WHITESPACE@46..47 " "
        AMP2@47..49 "&&"
        WHITESPACE@49..50 " "
        BIN_EXPR@50..61
          NAME_REF@50..56
            IDENT@50..56 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@56..57 " "
          LTGT@57..59 "<>"
          WHITESPACE@59..60 " "
          LITERAL@60..61
            LONG@60..61 "0"
    WHITESPACE@61..62 "\n"
    PIPE@62..63 "|"
    WHITESPACE@63..64 " "
    RENDER_OP@64..82
      IDENT@64..70 "render"
      WHITESPACE@70..71 " "
      IDENT@71..82 "columnchart"
    WHITESPACE@82..83 "\n"
    PIPE@83..84 "|"
    WHITESPACE@84..85 " "
    TAKE_OP@85..92
      IDENT@85..89 "take"
      WHITESPACE@89..90 " "
      LITERAL@90..92
        LONG@90..92 "10"
  WHITESPACE@92..93 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:2:20
  |
2 | | where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
  |                    ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `customerId == "c-001"`

error[DS0111]: `&&` is not an operator
  --> query:2:30
  |
2 | | where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
  |                              ^^ this is C's "and"
  |
  = help: use `and` to require both conditions

error[DS0107]: `<>` is not an operator
  --> query:2:40
  |
2 | | where customerId = "c-001" && amount <> 0
  |                                        ^^ this is SQL's "not equal"
  |
  = help: use `!=` to test that values differ: `amount != 0`

error[DS0120]: `render` must be the last operator
  --> query:3:3
  |
3 | | render columnchart
  |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the chart is drawn at this point
4 | | take 10
  |   ------- this operator comes after `render`
  |
  = help: move `render columnchart` to the end of the query

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv'
    | where customerId == "c-001" and amount != 0
    | take 10
    | render columnchart
which parses without errors
